    The condition for $m^{ed} \equiv m \pmod n$ for all $m$ is related to Euler's Totient Theorem.
    Euler's Totient Theorem states that if $\gcd(m, n) = 1$, then $m^{\phi(n)} \equiv 1 \pmod n$.
    In RSA, $n = pq$ where $p, q$ are distinct primes.
